Z||000002||shawnster69||08-15-2001||07:55 PM||||GO ahead and replace all the suspension parts!..all ball joints/struts/springs/steering shock and since you are working in that area make sure the calipers and rotors are in good shape..if not replace those too..just these few things..a couple hundred dollar job..the car will ride like brand new!! I did this to my 84 and couldn't believe the difference in handling..my 2 cents worth||||reg||6
Z||000003||Banzai||08-17-2001||03:08 AM||||I  have new KYB shocks and  struts for the car, New parking brake cables, I am  picking   up all the brake parts next week, new calipers,pads,rotors,and lines. I have a gasket set for the  motor, new plugs, wires, cap, rotor,fuel filter, wheel bearings, transmission  output shaft seals, steering stabilizer, sway bar busings, strut bumpers, door and  window switches, lock and ignition cylinders and keys, v-belts, clutch, etc,etc.<BR>I have to get new cradle bushings, exaust(Ocelot), starter(I cracked the solinoid trying to  take the  connections off). I am  planning on  putting in the performance cam, Holley throttle body,K+N, and I saw a site where a guy had Hooker  make a header for the car---looked trick.  I used to autocross a 94 Z28 and I had done  all the breathing mods to the motor-------what a difference. Man I miss that car.  The  short  block (Fiero)was replaced by GM at 56,000, the car has 101,000 on the chassis, body  is in great shape, underbody and floorboard  are very solid. picked the car up for 600 a year ago and drove it about 250 miles before the clutch let go. Any  help  would be greatly appreciated and if anyone has any other exaust options or performance parts for sale let me know<P>Banzai !!!!!!!!!||||reg||10
Z||000004||Tigger||08-17-2001||08:52 AM||||Search (click link in the upper right of this page) and dig up some existing threads on exhaust systems.  If that doesn't help, create a new thread asking about exhaust systems, it's unlikely those who know will look here.<P>I went with stock duals on my SE and they look and sound good.<P>I live probably only 15-20 minutes away so if you want to meet up, talk Fieros or need an extra hand at replacing all that stuff, hey get a hold of me.<P>P.S. Make sure you have enough Mt. Dew and pizza.  j/k  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
